# Line endings: LF in the working tree on EVERY OS.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a Windows clone checks every
# text file out with CRLF. Tests here read their own sources and fixtures as bytes — the
# no-console-window guard scans `src-tauri/src`, the transcript parser reads JSONL fixtures,
# contract goldens compare exact text — so a Windows checkout would test different bytes from the
# ones the Mac tests. One rule, one set of bytes, everywhere. The repository content was already
# LF; this changes only what a Windows working tree holds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe batch files are the exception: `cmd` mis-parses labels and `goto` in LF files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
